{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XhZ5tCL2m9G3CcNLrgew2j","type":"tool_result","content":"CONTEXT.md\ncritiques.md\nexisting_hypotheses.md\nrefinement_menu.md\nscratch\n441489      114  0.0  0.0 113420  1596 ?        Ss   09:52   0:00 /bin/bash -c source /home/users/kushinm/.claude/shell-snapshots/snapshot-bash-1791305530283-85unqo.sh 2>/dev/null || true && shopt -u extglob 2>/dev/null || true && { \\builtin unalias -- 'unsetenv'; \\builtin unset -f -- 'unsetenv'; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || true && eval 'cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; D=iter_4/candidate_5; ls $D; cp models/thurstonian_probit_decision.py $D/candidate.py; python3 - <<'\"'\"'EOF'\"'\"' p=\"iter_4/candidate_5/candidate.py\" s=open(p).read() old_head='\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"'\"\"\"Thurstonian (Gaussian-noise, probit) decision rule on the incumbent'\"'\"'s evidence. '\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"' new_head='\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"'\"\"\"Fitted-concentration trick coin in the Thurstonian (probit) randomness judgment.  Refinement of `thurstonian_probit_decision` (described below). Single change: the trick coin people suspect no longer has a fixed-concentration prior over its heads rate, Beta(2 s, 2 (1 - s)), but Beta(kappa s, kappa (1 - s)) with the concentration kappa fitted. kappa < 2 means people imagine trick coins as grossly lopsided, so only extreme head/tail imbalance is explained away as rigging and a moderately lopsided but switchy sequence is still credited as random; kappa > 2 means they imagine mildly biased coins. Addresses the critique that in length-8 pairs where the more-switching sequence is also the more lopsided one, people choose the more-switching sequence more often than the model predicts (they weigh heads/tails balance against switching less).  Description of the refined model follows.  Thurstonian (Gaussian-noise, probit) decision rule on the incumbent'\"'\"'s evidence. '\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"' assert old_head in s; s=s.replace(old_head,new_head,1) old='\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"'    a_h = 2.0 * s_heads     a_t = 2.0 - a_h     seq_lbias = (         pt.gammaln(seq_heads + a_h) + pt.gammaln(seq_len - seq_heads + a_t)         - pt.gammaln(seq_len + 2.0)         - pt.gammaln(a_h) - pt.gammaln(a_t) + math.lgamma(2.0)     )'\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"' new='\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"'    # Fitted concentration kappa of the trick-coin prior (kappa = 2 recovers     # the refined model): small kappa, only grossly lopsided coins imagined.     log_kappa = pm.Normal(\"log_kappa\", mu=math.log(2.0), sigma=0.75)     kappa = pm.Deterministic(\"kappa\", pt.exp(log_kappa))     a_h = kappa * s_heads     a_t = kappa - a_h     seq_lbias = (         pt.gammaln(seq_heads + a_h) + pt.gammaln(seq_len - seq_heads + a_t)         - pt.gammaln(seq_len + kappa)         - pt.gammaln(a_h) - pt.gammaln(a_t) + pt.gammaln(kappa)     )'\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"' assert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1) open(p,\"w\").write(s) EOF cat > $D/model_name.txt <<'\"'\"'EOF'\"'\"' lopsided_trick_coin_probit EOF cat > $D/hypothesis.md <<'\"'\"'EOF'\"'\"' Refinement of `thurstonian_probit_decision` (people pick the sequence whose noisy felt randomness is larger — a probit comparison — where felt randomness is how much better their own second-order picture of a fair coin explains the sequence than the regular generators they suspect: a switch-biased coin, a heads-favoured trick coin and a repeating motif with slips, weighed per flip with pseudo-flip dilution, heavy-tailed signed person sensitivity and a side habit). The single change is in how lopsided people imagine a trick coin to be: instead of a fixed prior over its heads rate, how concentrated that prior is is fitted, so if people picture trick coins as grossly rigged, only an extreme heads/tails imbalance is explained away as rigging, and a moderately lopsided but frequently switching sequence still looks random. This addresses the critique that in long pairs where the more-switching sequence is also the more lopsided one, people choose the more-switching sequence more often than the best model predicts — they weigh heads/tails balance against switching less than it assumes. EOF cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5' && pwd -P >| /tmp/claude-301b-cwd\n441489      121 87.4  0.1 2464876 352044 ?      Rl   09:52  18:09 /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv\n441489      829  0.0  0.0 113288  1528 ?        Ss   10:08   0:00 /bin/bash -c source /home/users/kushinm/.claude/shell-snapshots/snapshot-bash-1791305530283-85unqo.sh 2>/dev/null || true && shopt -u extglob 2>/dev/null || true && { \\builtin unalias -- 'unsetenv'; \\builtin unset -f -- 'unsetenv'; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || true && eval 'sleep 290; tail -5 /tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/a0dbf71e-e1bc-43be-ae66-ad771a199989/tasks/bxbw2dsrt.output; ps aux | grep check_candidate | head -3' < /dev/null && pwd -P >| /tmp/claude-9473-cwd","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0dbf71e-e1bc-43be-ae66-ad771a199989","uuid":"436ea9a1-87f8-42c3-a0ef-1dbb80142f6c","timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:13:15.231Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"CONTEXT.md\ncritiques.md\nexisting_hyp